                <pb facs="0563" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11721: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow (Adams) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-18T12:00:00+08:00">January 18,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 18—6:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Yangtze Rapid Steamship Company lighter No. 2 was boarded and looted on
                    January 16 at Low Point. The master, an American citizen named Charles Baker
                    “presumably registered at the Shanghai Consulate General” and six Chinese were
                    taken ashore and are held by the bandits. The United States Ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi> is proceeding immediately to Low Point.
                    Legation and Shanghai informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
